From 7a2da4defd3208a1d9d5163bd2912ecd5f100c1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chao Chen <209239467+surlymochan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:45:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dev): bind the dev stack to loopback unless --lan is
 passed

bun run dev bound the local Auth API and Signal service to 0.0.0.0 whenever
the desktop app was part of the stack. The development Auth API returns
sign-in codes in its response (AUTH_EXPOSE_DEVELOPMENT_CODE=true), so anyone
on the same network could sign in to the local stack.

- The stack now binds 127.0.0.1 by default. --lan opts in to 0.0.0.0 for a
  physical phone.
- --lan refuses to start while AUTH_EXPOSE_DEVELOPMENT_CODE is on, both on
  the command line and where the bind is configured.
- A LAN stack skips the throwaway development account role, which needs an
  exposed sign-in code; setting OPENBOT_DEV_REMOTE_ROLE still wins.
- scripts/dev-lan-guard-smoke.ts (bun run test:dev-lan-guard) covers the
  defaults and refusals and writes .openbot-build/dev-lan-guard.json.
